  "practice": [
    "Say the ঙ sound like the ng at the end of sing, song, and long; produce it toward the back of the mouth.",
    "Practice common conjuncts: ঙ্ক = ঙ্ + ক as in অঙ্ক, ঙ্খ = ঙ্ + খ as in শঙ্খ, ঙ্গ = ঙ্ + গ as in সঙ্গে, and ঙ্ঘ as in লঙ্ঘন.",
    "Compare full consonant ঙ in আঙুল, বাঙালি, and ভাঙা with the smaller anusvara sign ং in রং, সংখ্যা, and সংগীত.",
    "Train your eyes to spot ঙ inside words because it rarely begins ordinary Bangla words: বাঙালি, আঙুল, আঙুর, অঙ্ক, সঙ্গে, ভাঙা, and ব্যাঙ.",
    "Use বাংলা, বাঙালি, আঙুল, আঙুর, অঙ্ক, সঙ্গে, সঙ্গী, ভাঙা, ব্যাঙ, and রঙিন as quick reading anchors.",
    "Recognize these phrases instantly: আমি বাংলা শিখছি, বাংলায় বলো, আমার সঙ্গে আসো, এটা কী রং, and আমার আঙুলে ব্যথা."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঙ is a Bangla consonant used for the ng sound heard in English sing or song. It rarely begins ordinary Bangla words and usually appears inside words, especially near ক, খ, গ, or ঘ.",
    "Common conjunct forms include ঙ্ক (ঙ্ + ক), ঙ্খ (ঙ্ + খ), ঙ্গ (ঙ্ + গ), and ঙ্ঘ (ঙ্ + ঘ).",
    "ঙ and ং are different: ঙ is a full consonant, while ং is anusvara, a special sign. Compare আঙুল, বাঙালি, and ভাঙা with রং, সংখ্যা, and সংগীত.",
    "Because ঙ rarely starts words, internal recognition is more useful than memorizing word-initial examples.",
    "Best words to memorize include বাংলা, বাঙালি, বাংলাদেশ, আঙুল, আঙুর, অঙ্ক, অঙ্গ, সঙ্গে, সঙ্গী, সংগীত, সংখ্যা, সংগ্রহ, সংগ্রাম, ভাঙা, ব্যাঙ, রঙিন, and আঙিনা."
  ]
